       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Order as written:** ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Usual limits for adults:** the maximum is about 800 mg per dose and 3,200 mg/day in a monitored setting. For OTC use it is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** it is double the daily maximum. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n1,600 mg may be a total daily dose, or a typo for 400 mg or 800 mg. Please confirm what you intended. Some examples:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you really do want 1,600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it as a note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
